<title>CHINA: Wah Lee says in share placement talks.</title>
<headline>Wah Lee says in share placement talks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wah Lee Resources Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday it has started negotiations with Chinese concern China Everbright Financial Holdings Ltd on a possible placing of Wah Lee shares.</p>
<p>Wah Lee, which distributes domestic appliances and lifestyle products in China, said in a statement the negotiations are in a preliminary stage and have not been finalised.</p>
<p>China Everbright Financial is wholly owned by Chinese firm China Everbright Holdings Co Ltd, the parent of China Everbright International Ltd, China Everbright Technology Ltd, and China Everbright-IHD Pacific Ltd.</p>
<p>Shares of Wah Lee, listed in January, rose HK$0.425 to close at HK$3.275 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
